{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2439","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2439","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2439\",\"parent_revision\":\"941aca28fc40b2869fcc6abff92b49cc66789abb81d38497df78e787740d4198\",\"root_revision\":\"941aca28fc40b2869fcc6abff92b49cc66789abb81d38497df78e787740d4198\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAfter session interruption, the orchestrator has no visibility into active SAM plan state. Resuming work requires manually calling sam_plan(action='status') before knowing whether tasks are in-flight, complete, or stuck. Without this check, the orchestrator makes incorrect dispatch decisions \u2014 as observed when T99 was re-dispatched despite having already completed hours earlier.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Verified facts (re-verified 2026-05-29):**\\n\\n- `bd prime` command: documented in `research/task-management/beads.md` lines 53-56 as generating ~1-2k token workflow context summary for injection into agent sessions. SOURCE: Read(`research/task-management/beads.md`) lines 50-60 (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n  - verdict: VERIFIED\\n  - claim: `bd prime` generates ~1-2k token context summary\\n  - evidence: \\\"bd prime command generates ~1-2k token workflow context summary for injection into agent sessions\\\"\\n  - source: `research/task-management/beads.md` lines 53-56\\n\\n- `sam_plan(action='list')` returns per-plan data \u2014 confirmed in `server.py` line 324 (`_sam_plan_list` function defined). SOURCE: Bash grep on `server.py` (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n  - verdict: VERIFIED\\n  - claim: `_sam_plan_list` function exists at line 324\\n  - evidence: grep output: \\\"324:def _sam_plan_list(config: ListPlansConfig, plan_dir: str) -> dict:\\\"\\n  - source: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` line 324\\n\\n- `sam_plan(action='status')` function exists \u2014 confirmed at `server.py` line 350. SOURCE: Bash grep on `server.py` (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n  - verdict: VERIFIED\\n  - claim: `_sam_plan_status` exists at line 350\\n  - evidence: grep output: \\\"350:def _sam_plan_status(plan: str, plan_dir: str) -> dict:\\\"\\n  - source: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` line 350\\n\\n- `sam_plan(action='ready')` function exists \u2014 confirmed at `server.py` line 368. SOURCE: Bash grep on `server.py` (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n  - verdict: VERIFIED\\n  - claim: `_sam_plan_ready` exists at line 368\\n  - evidence: grep output: \\\"368:def _sam_plan_ready(plan: str, config: ReadyPlanConfig, plan_dir: str) -> dict:\\\"\\n  - source: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` line 368\\n\\n- `last-activity` field on Task model \u2014 confirmed in `models.py` lines 157-162. SOURCE: Bash grep on `models.py` (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n  - verdict: VERIFIED\\n  - claim: `last_activity: datetime | None` exists on Task model with alias `last-activity`\\n  - evidence: grep output: \\\"157:    last_activity: datetime | None = Field(\\\", \\\"159:        validation_alias=AliasChoices('last-activity', 'last_activity')\\\"\\n  - source: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` lines 157-162\\n\\n- No existing `resume` action in SAM server \u2014 confirmed by grep returning no output. SOURCE: Bash grep for `action.*resume` on `sam_schema/` (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n  - verdict: VERIFIED\\n  - claim: No `resume` action currently exists in `action_models.py` or `server.py`\\n  - evidence: grep returned empty output for `action.*resume|resume.*action|action='resume'|action=\\\"resume\\\"` across `sam_schema/`\\n  - source: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/` (searched 2026-05-29)\\n\\n- `context-mode` plugin absent from repo \u2014 confirmed. SOURCE: Bash ls on `plugins/` (accessed 2026-05-28, re-confirmed 2026-05-29)\\n  - verdict: VERIFIED (absence confirmed)\\n  - claim: `plugins/context-mode/` does not exist; cannot use as implementation reference\\n  - evidence: plugin.json keys list confirms only sam-related MCP server present; no context-mode plugin found\\n  - source: `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Unverified claims:**\\n- `context-mode` plugin capabilities (`ctx_prime` or equivalent behavior) \u2014 referenced in item but plugin absent from repo. Cannot verify feature parity.\\n  - verdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\n  - claim: `bd prime` pattern can be directly mirrored in SAM\\n  - evidence: None \u2014 context-mode plugin not available in this codebase\\n  - source: N/A\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Priority**: P1\\n**Justification**: This item blocks every multi-session SAM feature implementation. The missing guardrail causes an error class (duplicate task dispatch, state corruption) that is easy to hit after session interruption and easy to miss without an automatic surface. The fix is small (Effort: Small) relative to the blast radius.\\n**Effort**: Small \u2014 composes 3 existing MCP actions (sam_plan list, sam_plan status, sam_plan ready) into a single resume call. Implementation estimate: 1 new MCP action or 1 skill file + update to implement-feature SKILL.md. No schema changes. No new dependencies.\\n**Timing**: No hard deadline. Should precede any SAM multi-session work to prevent recurrence of the T99 re-dispatch class of error.\\n**Priority signals**: Error observed in production (plan Pdec8934d, 2026-05-15). Effort:benefit ratio is strongly favorable (Small effort, eliminates a recurring-risk error class). Unblocks downstream implement-feature improvement.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Blocks**: Every multi-session SAM feature implementation where work spans more than one Claude Code session\\n- **Bottleneck**: Orchestrators resuming work must manually call `sam_plan status` before any dispatch decision \u2014 this is an easy step to forget, especially when resuming after an interruption\\n- **Error class**: Duplicate task dispatch wastes compute, can produce conflicting outputs or merge conflicts, and corrupts plan state (task marked complete is re-dispatched and status transitions back to in-progress)\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Eliminates the class of re-dispatch bugs caused by stale orchestrator memory at session resume\\n- Gives orchestrators a zero-friction entry point: single call produces actionable context (what to do next)\\n- Mirrors `bd prime` pattern which is documented as generating ~1-2k token context summary \u2014 compact enough for automatic injection at session start\\n- Enables the implement-feature skill to be safely resumed without any manual status gathering step\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an orchestrator resumes work on a SAM plan after a session interruption, invoking the resume tool/skill produces a structured context summary covering: all plans currently tracked, per-plan task counts by status (complete/in-progress/not-started/blocked), identification of any in-progress tasks that appear stalled (no activity for a configurable threshold), and the concrete next action the orchestrator should take (e.g., dispatch ready tasks, investigate blocked tasks, or confirm the plan is complete).\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA session-resume context surface for SAM plans that:\\n- Is invocable as a single call (one skill load or one MCP tool call) without parameters when used for general resume\\n- Returns structured output the orchestrator can parse without natural language interpretation\\n- Covers all active plans (not just a named one) when called without a plan argument\\n- Identifies tasks in ambiguous states: in-progress with no recent activity (stalled), blocked with no unblock path documented\\n- Provides a recommended next action per plan\\n- Stays within the context budget documented for bd prime (~1-2k tokens)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Calling the resume tool/skill with no arguments returns a summary of all plans in the current project's plan directory, including task counts by status for each plan\\n2. Any task in `in-progress` status with `last-activity` older than a configurable threshold (default: configurable, minimum: clock-based) is flagged as stalled in the output\\n3. For each plan, the output includes a `next_action` field: one of `dispatch` (ready tasks exist), `investigate` (blocked or stalled tasks exist with no ready tasks), or `complete` (all tasks terminal)\\n4. The total token count of the output for a typical plan (20 tasks) is below 2000 tokens (verified by encoding with cl100k_base)\\n5. The resume tool/skill can be invoked at the start of an implement-feature session and its output used directly to skip the manual `sam_plan(action='status')` + `sam_plan(action='ready')` two-step\\n6. Re-dispatching an already-complete task does not occur in a session that loaded the resume context before dispatching\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| MCP tool | `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_plan` \u2014 all existing plan actions |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 SAM MCP server; `_sam_plan_list`, `_sam_plan_status`, `_sam_plan_ready` |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `Task.last_activity` field, `TaskStatus` enum, `PlanState` enum |\\n| Skill | `/dh:implement-feature` \u2014 primary consumer; progress loop needs updating |\\n| Research | `research/task-management/beads.md` \u2014 `bd prime` pattern reference (lines 53\u201356) |\\n| Skill | `/dh:planner-rt-ica` \u2014 used during grooming |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 `last-activity` field already exists on Task model; all required MCP actions exist\\n- Blocks: `/dh:implement-feature` session-resume improvement (the implement-feature skill would call this new tool to avoid manual status gathering)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the data is already available via three existing MCP actions (`list`, `status`, `ready`). The implementation composes them into a single call. Stall detection adds a small amount of logic against the existing `last-activity` timestamp field. Estimated as: 1 MCP action addition (or 1 skill file), plus update to implement-feature SKILL.md. No schema changes required.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 instructs agents on session resume; current instruction does not include resume state check\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` \u2014 dispatching agents reference `sam_plan`; should mention pre-dispatch state check\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 references sam_plan for task orchestration; should note resume pattern at session start\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- `context-mode` plugin referenced in item is absent from repo \u2014 cannot use it as implementation reference. Design must be self-contained within the SAM server.\\n- Three design decisions require human input before execution (see Questions for Human)\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 progress loop must call resume action at session start; line 289 currently notes plan can be resumed but provides no automatic state surface\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` \u2014 line 111 references sam_plan; should note resume action as pre-dispatch check\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py` \u2014 `PlanConfig` discriminated union (line 322) must include new `ResumeConfig` when delivery form is MCP action\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/` \u2014 new test file needed for resume action (verify stall detection, next_action values, token budget)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 may need `resume` read path if logic requires cross-plan aggregation beyond what `list`+`status`+`ready` provide\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::sam_plan` \u2014 new `action='resume'` handler (or new `sam_resume` tool); composes `_sam_plan_list`, `_sam_plan_status`, `_sam_plan_ready` into single response\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/action_models.py::ResumeConfig` \u2014 new Pydantic model for resume action (or new tool schema); must be added to discriminated union `PlanConfig`\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 existing pytest job at line 267 covers `plugins/development-harness/tests/`; new `tests_sam/` test for resume action will be picked up automatically by pytest discovery if added to `tests_sam/`\\n- No new CI configuration required\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe feature aligns with the SAM methodology's core principle: every stage produces a named artifact that enables stateless handoff. Session resume without state context violates statelessness \u2014 the orchestrator is forced to carry implicit memory of plan state across session boundaries rather than querying durable plan state. This feature restores the stateless contract at the session boundary.\\n\\nWave 2 alignment verification (2026-05-29):\\n- SAM stateless principle confirmed: `sam_plan` MCP tool already provides `list`, `status`, `ready` actions \u2014 the resume surface composes these rather than adding state. No state is added to the server. ALIGNED.\\n- Gap confirmed real: no `resume` action in `action_models.py` (grep verified). The missing guardrail is genuine. ALIGNED.\\n- `last_activity` field already exists on Task model (models.py:157) \u2014 stall detection requires no schema change. ALIGNED with \\\"no schema changes required\\\" scope statement.\\n- The feature does NOT add implementation-prescriptive architecture \u2014 delivery form (MCP action vs skill) remains a planning decision. ALIGNED with grooming scope boundary.\\n\\nNo divergence found. The feature as specified restores the stateless handoff contract without adding new persistent state.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/sam-definition.md` \u2014 should reference the resume surface as part of SAM stateless contract\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 progress loop section needs update to show resume call pattern\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: No guardrail exists at session start or resume that surfaces SAM plan state. The orchestrator has no enforcement point that prevents it from making dispatch decisions on stale plan state. The observed failure mode (T99 re-dispatched after completion, plan `Pdec8934d`, 2026-05-15) is exactly the class of error a guardrail prevents \u2014 a system gate that should have checked plan state before dispatch was absent. The failure is not a defect in existing code but an absent mechanism.\\n**Analysis Method**: missing-guardrail (no root-cause analysis required \u2014 the guardrail itself is the deliverable)\\n**Scenario Target**: Session resume without plan state \u2192 incorrect dispatch decisions \u2192 duplicate task execution and state corruption\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Observed: 2026-05-15 during implement-feature orchestration for plan `Pdec8934d` \u2014 T99 was re-dispatched despite having completed hours earlier\\n- Root cause: No automatic state surface at session resume; orchestrator relied on in-session memory that did not persist across the interruption\\n- Source: Item context field: `Session observation \u2014 2026-05-15, implement-feature orchestration for Pdec8934d`\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n1. **Delivery form**: Should this be (a) a new `action='resume'` on the existing `sam_plan` MCP tool, (b) a new standalone MCP tool `sam_resume`, or (c) a skill that composes existing sam_plan calls? Option (a) keeps the surface area minimal; option (c) avoids touching the MCP server.\\n2. **Stall threshold**: What constitutes a \\\"stalled\\\" in-progress task? A fixed time threshold (e.g., >2 hours since `last-activity`)? Or is stall detection optional/out of scope for v1?\\n3. **Scope \u2014 single plan vs all plans**: Should the resume surface all plans at once (global resume) or require a plan address (per-plan resume)? The item description says \\\"which plans exist\\\" suggesting global, but the implement-feature use case is per-plan.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: bd prime equivalent for SAM plans\\nDate: 2026-05-29\\nGoal: Add a single-call session-resume surface for SAM plans that eliminates incorrect dispatch decisions after session interruption\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent (what the feature must do) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description and acceptance criteria are specific and complete \u2014 6 verifiable ACs present\\n2. External interfaces (sam_plan list/status/ready) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Bash grep confirmed _sam_plan_list at server.py:324, _sam_plan_status at :350, _sam_plan_ready at :368 (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n3. Task model field (last-activity for stall detection) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Bash grep confirmed last_activity: datetime | None = Field( at models.py:157 with alias last-activity (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n4. No existing resume action (implementation gap confirmed) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Bash grep for action.*resume on sam_schema/ returned empty \u2014 no resume action exists (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n5. bd prime token budget (~1-2k tokens) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Bash read of beads.md lines 50-60 confirmed bd prime command generates ~1-2k token workflow context summary (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n6. Delivery form (MCP action vs standalone tool vs skill) | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: MISSING | Citation: Three valid options exist (a) action=resume on sam_plan, (b) new sam_resume tool, (c) skill \u2014 design choice with trade-offs; no codebase evidence selects one. Cannot derive from code.\\n7. Stall threshold definition | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | Citation: No stall threshold defined anywhere in codebase. grep for threshold/stall on sam_schema/ returned no results (accessed 2026-05-29). Requires human decision.\\n8. Output format specification | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | Citation: ACs specify next_action field values and token limit but not the full structured output schema. Format details are a design decision.\\n9. context-mode pattern reference | Snapshot: PARTIAL \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Citation: context-mode plugin absent from repo (confirmed 2026-05-29). bd prime is a reference pattern only.\\n10. Scope (global all-plans vs per-plan) | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: MISSING | Citation: ACs say all plans in the current project plan directory (global) but Questions for Human flag this as unresolved.\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 6 (delivery form): DERIVABLE \u2192 MISSING (three equal-weight options, no codebase signal)\\n- Condition 9 (context-mode pattern): PARTIAL \u2192 DERIVABLE (absent plugin is not a blocker; design self-contained)\\n- Condition 10 (scope single vs all): confirmed MISSING from explicit Questions for Human\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 3\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\nNote: The 3 MISSING conditions are design decisions (delivery form, stall threshold, scope). They do not block grooming \u2014 they are documented as Questions for Human for resolution at planning phase.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Start a SAM plan with `sam_plan(action='create', ...)` and dispatch tasks\\n2. Allow tasks to reach various states: complete, in-progress, blocked\\n3. Terminate the Claude Code session (close terminal or let it time out)\\n4. Start a new Claude Code session\\n5. Attempt to continue work on the plan \u2014 orchestrator has no visibility into task states without first calling `sam_plan(action='status', plan='P{N}')`\\n6. Dispatch a task without checking status \u2014 observe that already-complete tasks can be re-dispatched\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n1. `sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 SAM MCP server; provides all plan actions; primary implementation target\\n2. `sam_schema/core/action_models.py` \u2014 discriminated union for plan/task/active-task actions; must add ResumeConfig\\n3. `sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Task model with `last_activity: datetime | None` (lines 157-162); stall detection reads this field\\n4. `sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 task and plan read operations; used by list/status/ready; resume aggregates their outputs\\n5. `tests_sam/` \u2014 existing SAM test suite; new test file for resume action\\n6. `skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 primary consumer skill; progress loop needs update\\n7. `skills/dispatch/SKILL.md` \u2014 references sam_plan; secondary consumer\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **bd prime equivalent for sam plans** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-05-15, implement-feature orchestration for Pdec8934d\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f1b057ad65dcf87762e0ceacff57305adf2255fff401b7aef40d9feb744bdfb3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTAU6A\"}"}